Spoilers Ahead

While in a little trip through the dungeon (albeit in discovery mode)
I found some neat little tricks for using Wishes.

One of the first things you *should* wish for is 3 (count 'em) blessed
luckstones.  These *really* help out, both in general play and getting
your wishes granted.

The next thing I wished for was a blessed magic lamp.  If you rub this,
eventually a demon appears and grants you one wish (I never had anything
else happen, and I haven't looked in the code, but I tried this several
times and nothing different happened!!).  

The next thing to wish for is 3 (there is that magic number again!) blessed
scrolls of charging.  Assuming you get all three (thats where the luckstones
come in handy!), you can recharge the wand of wishing (you can only do this 
once) and you can recharge the magic lamp (It doesn't seem to have any    
recharge limit, although again I didn't check the code).  With the second
charges on the wand of wishing, you can get all of those neat little goodies
like Stormbringer, amulets of live saving, ect.

Hope this helps ---     

